-- title:
--   Order of uvarpi^mρ' downstairs: equality iff base change bijective
-- statement:
--   All five rings lie in one universe. Let $R'$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K'$ and let $\varpi \in R'$ generate its maximal ideal; let $O'$ be an $R'$-algebra which is a domain, and let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain which is an $R'$-algebra such that $\operatorname{algebraMap} R' O$ is a local homomorphism and $\mathfrak m_{R'}O = \mathfrak m_O$; let $O$ be an $O'$-algebra compatibly over $R'$, and let $F$ be a field which is a fraction field of $O$ and of $O'$ and a $K'$-algebra, all the algebra structures forming scalar towers over $R'$. Let $d \in \mathbb N$, let $b'$ be an $O'$-basis of $\Omega_{O'/R'}$ and $b$ an $O$-basis of $\Omega_{O/R'}$, both indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, let $m \in \mathbb Z$, $u \in O'^{\times}$, and let $\sigma \in \bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K'}$ satisfy $\sigma = (u\,\varpi^{m})\cdot\rho'$, where the scalar is the product in $F$ of the image of $u$ and the $m$-th power of the image of $\varpi$, and $\rho' = \mathtt{topFormMap}\,R'\,K'\,O'\,F\,d$ applied to the wedge of $b'$, i.e. the image of $b'_1\wedge\cdots\wedge b'_d$ in $\bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K'}$. Here $\mathtt{ord}\,R'\,K'\,O\,d\,F\,\omega$ is defined, whenever the $O$-submodule $\mathtt{integralTopForms}$ (the image of $\bigwedge^d_O\Omega_{O/R'}$ in $\bigwedge^d_F\Omega_{F/K'}$) is generated by a single $\rho$ with $\omega = a\cdot\rho$ for some $a \in F$, as $\mathtt{addOrd}\,O\,F\,a$ for a chosen such witness $a$ (and as $0$ otherwise), $\mathtt{addOrd}$ being the additive valuation attached to the discrete valuation ring $O$ on $F$ (with value $0$ at $0$). The conclusion is that $m \le \mathtt{ord}\,R'\,K'\,O\,d\,F\,\sigma$, and that equality holds if and only if `KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange R' O' O` $\colon O \otimes_{O'} \Omega_{O'/R'} \to \Omega_{O/R'}$ is bijective.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic comparison of orders of top-degree differential forms along a birational map of smooth models, in the style of the treatment of weak Néron models in Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud. It is the common ingredient of the component-reading results [`NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.eq_n_of_forall_topFormMap_eq_mul_zpow_smul`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.eq_n_of_forall_topFormMap_eq_mul_zpow_smul) and [`NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.n_le_n_and_isOpenImmersion_of_n_eq_of_specializes`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.n_le_n_and_isOpenImmersion_of_n_eq_of_specializes), and of [`NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.eq_addOrd_and_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_topFormMap_eq_of_addOrd_le`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.eq_addOrd_and_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_topFormMap_eq_of_addOrd_le).
